{"name":"Bootstrap Leather","hex":"#793721","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bootstrap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A loop (leather or other material) sewn at the side or top rear of a boot to help in pulling the boot on.","A means of advancing oneself or accomplishing something without aid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To help (oneself) without the aid of others.","To load the operating system into the memory of a computer. Usually shortened to boot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bootstrap"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The most common leathers come from cattle, sheep, goats, equine animals, buffalo, pigs and hogs, ostriches, and aquatic animals such as seals and alligators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Leathertools.jpg/330px-Leathertools.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather","wikidata":"Q286"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Ledertrocknung_in_Suai.jpg/500px-Ledertrocknung_in_Suai.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Ledertrocknun